# FACT-AI Bilinear MLP Interpretability Project

## Project Identity

**Course**: FACT-AI (Fairness, Accountability, Confidentiality and Transparency in AI), UvA MSc AI  
**Paper**: "Bilinear MLPs enable weight-based mechanistic interpretability" (arXiv:2410.08417)  
**Deadline**: 30 January 2026  
**Result Freeze**: 17 January 2026

**Reproduction Scope**:
- Section 4 (Vision): MNIST/Fashion-MNIST eigendecomposition
- Section 5 (Language): Negation circuit discovery via SAE analysis

---

## Research Questions & Extensions

### Core Hypothesis
> **Structural low-rank** (CP-Decomposition) produces equivalent or better interpretability than **emergent low-rank** (via regularization), with the advantage of explicit rank control.

### Research Questions / Extensions

| ID | Extension | Goal |
|----|-----------|------|
| RQ1 | Regularization vs. Interpretability | How does training regularization (none vs. noise vs. weight decay) affect eigenvalue spectrum rank and eigenvector interpretability? Does regularization lead to cleaner, more interpretable features? |
| RQ2 | Cross-Dataset Robustness | Do learned eigenvectors generalize beyond the training distribution (Rotated MNIST, EMNIST)? Do perturbations remain class-targeted, or do eigenvectors reflect dataset artifacts? |
| RQ3 | Forced Low-Rank (CP Factorization) | Does forcing low-rank structure via CP decomposition improve interpretability compared to emergent low-rank behavior? Is low rank necessary or merely sufficient for interpretability? |
| RQ4 | Regularization vs. Structural Rank | How do emergent low-rank (from regularization) and explicit rank constraints (CP) compare in terms of performance, robustness, and interpretability trade-offs? |
| RQ5 | Architectural Scalability (Conceptual) | How could bilinear interaction constraints scale to larger vision models (Tucker-factorized layers)? What are the parameter scaling and interpretability trade-offs? |

### Key Comparisons to Make
- Dense (no reg) vs Dense (full reg) vs CP R=32 (no reg)
- Accuracy vs Effective Rank Pareto frontier
- Eigenvector quality side-by-side

