## Critical Constraints

### 1. Original Code Preservation
```
bilinear-decomposition-main/   ← DO NOT MODIFY
```
This directory contains the original paper code. All our implementations WRAP this code (don't reimplement).

### 2. Environmental Tracking (MANDATORY)
Every experiment MUST log:
- GPU hours (`wall_time * gpu_count`)
- CO2 emissions via `codecarbon`
- All metrics to wandb

### 3. Snellius HPC Specifics
```bash
ssh scur0075@Snellius  # Case-sensitive hostname
#SBATCH --partition=gpu_a100
module load 2025
module load Anaconda3/2025.06-1
source activate fact
```

### 4. Budget Awareness
- Total budget: 25,000 SBUs
- Always test locally before cluster submission
- Claude outputs job files; humans submit manually

### 5. Reproducibility
- All experiments use 5 seeds: `[42, 43, 44, 45, 46]`
- Configs stored in `configs/` as YAML

